1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:10,556
Speaking, task one. Topic 1: About me. Ten questions. Listen to the question and answer out loud.

2
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:12,526
What is your name?

3
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:21,709
My name is Oleh Kovalenko. My friends call me Olek.

4
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,663
Where are you from?

5
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:33,324
I am from Ukraine, from the city of Kharkiv. It is a big city in the east.

6
00:00:34,233 --> 00:00:35,511
Where do you live now?

7
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,748
Now I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou with my family.

8
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:46,146
How long have you been in Czechia?

9
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:55,396
I have been in Czechia for five years. I came in 2021.

10
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,393
What do you do?

11
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,809
I work in a warehouse and in my free time I learn Czech.

12
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,503
What languages do you speak?

13
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,250
I speak Ukrainian, Russian and a little Czech and English.

14
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:19,443
What kind of person are you?

15
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:28,645
I think I am calm and friendly. I like helping people.

16
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,623
What did you do before you came to Czechia?

17
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:39,605
In Ukraine I worked as a shop assistant.

18
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,022
Why did you come to Czechia?

19
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:50,616
I came because of work and because my relatives live here.

20
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,280
What would you like to do in five years?

21
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:01,993
In five years I would like to have a better job and speak Czech well.

22
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:11,717
Speaking, task one. Topic 2: Family. Ten questions. Listen to the question and answer out loud.

23
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:14,106
How many people are there in your family?

24
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:23,264
There are four of us: my wife, two sons and me.

25
00:02:24,166 --> 00:02:25,505
Do you have any brothers or sisters?

26
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:35,738
Yes, I have one brother. He is three years older and lives in Ukraine.

27
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:38,162
Where do your parents live?

28
00:02:43,566 --> 00:02:46,481
My parents live in Ukraine in a small town by a river.

29
00:02:47,366 --> 00:02:49,733
What does your husband or wife do?

30
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,098
My wife works in a hospital as a nurse.

31
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,557
How old are your children?

32
00:03:05,966 --> 00:03:10,138
My son is nine and my daughter is five. My son is in the third year at school.

33
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:12,883
What do you like doing as a family?

34
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:21,509
As a family we like going for walks and at the weekend we play games.

35
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,165
How often do you call your parents?

36
00:03:29,566 --> 00:03:32,706
I call my parents almost every evening when they are at home.

37
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,370
When did you last see your parents?

38
00:03:40,766 --> 00:03:44,649
I last saw my parents last summer when they came to visit.

39
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:47,900
How did you celebrate the last birthday in your family?

40
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:57,144
Last month we had a party at home for our son with a cake and friends.

41
00:03:58,033 --> 00:03:59,785
Where will you go with your family next time?

42
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,930
Next summer we will go to the sea in Croatia with the family.

43
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:18,513
Speaking, task two. Card number 1. You are at the post office. You want to send a parcel abroad. Ask four questions.

44
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:22,433
You are at the post office. You want to send a parcel abroad.

45
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:26,128
Hello. What can I do for you?

46
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:35,085
Hello, I want to send a parcel to Ukraine. How much does it cost?

47
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,733
A parcel up to 5 kilograms costs 650 CZK.

48
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:45,283
How long does it take?

49
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,258
The parcel will be there in about five days.

50
00:04:52,466 --> 00:04:54,087
Can I pay by card?

51
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,993
Yes, you can pay by card or in cash.

52
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,933
Can I track the parcel online?

53
00:05:04,133 --> 00:05:06,689
Yes, you will find the tracking number on the receipt.

54
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,900
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

55
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,866
You're welcome. Goodbye.

56
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:21,939
Speaking, task two. Card number 2. You are at a language school. You want to sign up for an English course. Ask four questions.

57
00:05:22,633 --> 00:05:26,428
You are at a language school. You want to sign up for an English course.

58
00:05:27,633 --> 00:05:30,128
Hello. What can I do for you?

59
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:37,896
Hello, when does the English course start?

60
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,200
The new course starts on 1 October.

61
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,433
How much is it?

62
00:05:46,633 --> 00:05:49,594
The course costs 4,500 CZK per term.

63
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,587
How many people are in the group?

64
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:59,222
There are at most ten people in the group.

65
00:06:04,433 --> 00:06:05,566
Is the course in the evening?

66
00:06:05,766 --> 00:06:08,685
Yes, the lessons are always on Tuesday at 6 pm.

67
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:11,900
Thank you for the information. Goodbye.

68
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,866
You're welcome. Goodbye.

69
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:24,644
Speaking, task three. Story number 1: Moving house. What did the Novák family do yesterday? Tell the story from the pictures in the past tense.

70
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:27,358
What did the Novák family do yesterday?

71
00:06:48,066 --> 00:06:50,864
Yesterday the Novák family moved to a new flat.

72
00:06:51,066 --> 00:06:53,100
In the morning they packed everything into boxes.

73
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:56,033
Mum packed the dishes and the children packed the toys.

74
00:06:56,233 --> 00:06:58,000
Then a big van arrived.

75
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,166
Two strong men carried the boxes and furniture to the van.

76
00:07:01,366 --> 00:07:03,833
It was hard, but it went quickly.

77
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:06,722
In the new flat they put the sofa and the table in place.

78
00:07:06,933 --> 00:07:10,161
Dad put the beds together and Mum cleaned the kitchen.

79
00:07:10,366 --> 00:07:12,333
In the evening everyone was very tired.

80
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:14,900
They had no time to cook, so they ordered pizza.

81
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:17,600
They ate it on the floor between the boxes and laughed.

82
00:07:17,933 --> 00:07:28,165
Speaking, task three. Story number 2: A trip to the mountains. What did Petr and Jana do on Saturday? Tell the story from the pictures in the past tense.

83
00:07:28,866 --> 00:07:30,612
What did Petr and Jana do on Saturday?

84
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:53,866
On Saturday Petr and Jana went on a trip to the mountains.

85
00:07:54,066 --> 00:07:56,587
In the morning they sat on the train and looked out of the window.

86
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,017
It was nice outside and the sun was shining.

87
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:01,725
Then they walked up the path to the top of the hill.

88
00:08:01,933 --> 00:08:04,833
The way was long, but the nature was beautiful.

89
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:06,633
Suddenly it started to rain.

90
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:10,200
Petr and Jana had no umbrella, so they got completely wet.

91
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,058
Finally they found a small hut.

92
00:08:12,266 --> 00:08:14,466
They sat down at the table and drank hot tea.

93
00:08:14,666 --> 00:08:17,266
They rested and waited for the rain to stop.

94
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:28,243
Speaking, task four. Situation number 1. The examiner describes a situation. Agree with her, choose one option and say why.

95
00:08:28,934 --> 00:08:37,639
Our friend has a birthday soon. We want to buy her a present together. What shall we buy her? Any ideas? You can choose from these options.

96
00:08:46,334 --> 00:08:47,905
We can buy her a book.

97
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,707
I think she already has the book. She doesn't read much.

98
00:08:50,999 --> 00:08:52,693
Then let's buy her chocolate.

99
00:08:52,999 --> 00:08:55,501
Not chocolate, she doesn't eat sweets now.

100
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,436
OK, then let's buy her flowers.

101
00:08:58,734 --> 00:09:00,340
And why do you want to buy that?

102
00:09:00,634 --> 00:09:03,167
Because she likes flowers and they will make her happy.

103
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:07,064
That's true, flowers are a good idea. Let's buy her flowers.

104
00:09:07,467 --> 00:09:17,470
Speaking, task four. Situation number 2. The examiner describes a situation. Agree with her, choose one option and say why.

105
00:09:18,167 --> 00:09:25,040
On Saturday evening we want to go out together. Where shall we go? Any ideas? You can choose from these options.

106
00:09:33,734 --> 00:09:35,256
How about going to the cinema?

107
00:09:35,567 --> 00:09:38,026
I don't feel like the cinema, I was there yesterday.

108
00:09:38,334 --> 00:09:39,749
Then we can go to the theatre.

109
00:09:40,034 --> 00:09:41,380
The theatre is too expensive.

110
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:43,175
Then let's go to a restaurant.

111
00:09:43,467 --> 00:09:44,983
And why do you want to go there?

112
00:09:45,267 --> 00:09:47,925
Because we are hungry and we can talk there in peace.

113
00:09:48,234 --> 00:09:51,963
OK, that's a good idea. Let's go to a restaurant.

114
00:09:52,267 --> 00:10:01,223
Practise situation 2 on the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website. The link is in the video description. And subscribe — a new video every day.
